                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This has the most schizophrenic UI since clippy.  2.1 hours on record and at least 1.5 of those has been wandering around menus trying to do basic things that shouldn't take 5 minutes.  Want to change the stock betaflight osd with the horizon on it?  Just jump in the OSD editor under tools, right?  Seems easy enough, edit it, save it, strange that it didn't ask me to assign it to a quad but who knows maybe it's universal?  Jump in a race, and nope, didn't work.  Well, okay, it seems to do everything on a per quad basis so maybe go into the quad builder and assign it under the flight controller settings.  Nope, can't find it.  Have to exit the game and go ask google, turns out it's buried in the game options under the general options menu.  Gee, thanks.  FYI, same place you have to go to change how many bots, if any, you want in a race.  Go to setup a race and think you'd find it there?  Nope, options menu.\n\nAudio?  Music blasting away?  Check.  Sound effects in menu?  Check.  Hmm, why is my quad silent?  Does the game just not have propeller sound?  Well, maybe it's realistic and you only hear the quad flying from wherever \"you're\" standing?  Try flying by the character model?  Nope, still don't hear it.  Exit the game, more googling, game might be having some audio issues with 5.1?  Check all that, disable a bunch of audio outputs, go back in the game?  Nothing.  Well, let me turn off this obnoxiously loud music anyway...  Go back to flying, barely hear the humming of props...  Was it drivers?  Was it just inaudible otherwise?  No idea.  Another 20 minutes down the drain.\n\nThen there doesn't seem to be any leaderboards for doing time trials but who knows.  There could be for all I know.  Maybe somewhere in the audio options, or who else knows where.\n\nI wish DRL was still supported.\n\nOnly recommended at this point because I feel like I haven't given it enough of a chance.",
